# Whatnot CSV characters (standing order)

**When this applies:** Any time Steve asks for **characters** on a **Whatnot CSV** (new show upload, inventory Whatnot, $15 boards, CTR leftover BIN, rebuild titles, etc.).

**Default:** Use `Cursor Projects/WhatnotCharacterPipeline/` end-to-end. Do not invent a one-off image-only VLM path unless he explicitly says image-only or there is no pricing title source.

## Hard isolation

- Implement under `Cursor Projects/<WhatnotProject>/` only (plus ClickToClaim crop publish folders when asked).
- Do **not** edit pricing watchers, PrepareClickToClaim, CTR inbox/LaunchAgents, PinPricingStudyMVP production, or Application Support mirrors.
- Do **not** add VLM/character logic into those systems. Import or copy from `WhatnotCharacterPipeline/`.

## Required steps

1. **Titles into VLM (priced/CTR):** Set `ebay_title` from pricing (`listing_title` or `selected_candidate.title`). Image-only only when no title exists.
2. **Hybrid pick:** `character_pick.pick_character(...)` (title fills empty/low/disagree; VLM wins on clear crop mismatch; fallback `Disney Pin`).
3. **Review gate:** Contact sheet + editable review → `character_map_for_whatnot.json` → build CSV from that map.
4. **Flag:** empty/generic, low confidence, A2Z boards, subject labels, title/VLM hard disagree, missing ebay title.

## $15 / no-pricing

Image-only VLM is OK; still run contact-sheet review before upload when time allows.

